      "rationale": "18 distinct stories in the story map, five of which carry 7+ sources, with significant developments across three of five signal categories. The domestic regime dimension is the most active: four simultaneous pressure vectors (LRT 30,000-person protest, PM competence crisis from interview backlash, Paluckas immunity request, coalition polling at 48.2%). Security produces a concrete legislative action (Kapčiamiestis 105-12-4 Seimas vote). Alignment produces the Cyprus EU summit as substantive multilateral output. The two highest-prominence stories (Stories #1 and #6, 12 sources each) reflect genuinely different dimensions — one a domestic governance legitimacy crisis, the other Lithuania's active participation in reshaping EU defense architecture. Economic activity is elevated above baseline by pension reform data (40% withdrawal) but does not cross into structural posture change. Note on Story #7 (11 sources, EU Article 42.7 debate): this story's prominence reflects a major European-level development in which Lithuania is an active participant rather than a spectator; it is assessed under alignment and institutional but is not solely a Lithuanian story, which appropriately limits its weight in the posture assessment."
